              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "dersom",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", and "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " can introduce the condition. For unreal past situations, the condition often uses past perfect (had done, called "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "pluskvamperfektum",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " in Norwegian), while the result uses the conditional perfect."
            }
